AAC-LC fixtures, made with ffmpeg 9.0.2 (its native `aac` encoder, LGPL-2.1+,
from synthetic signals generated by lavfi: nothing of anyone's recording).
Each is ADTS (`-f adts`), one second long.

  S=aevalsrc=exprs=0.4*sin(2*PI*440*t)+0.3*sin(2*PI*3000*t)*lt(mod(t\,0.25)\,0.01)+0.05*random(0):d=1:s=44100:c=stereo
  st44.aac          ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "$S" -c:a aac -b:a 96k -f adts
  st44-tools.aac    the same with -aac_pns 1 -aac_tns 1 -aac_is 1 -aac_ms 1
  mono22.aac        440 Hz sine plus noise, mono, 22050 Hz, -b:a 32k
  surround51.aac    six sines and noise, 5.1, 48000 Hz, -b:a 256k
  mono8.aac         440 Hz sine plus noise, mono, 8000 Hz, -b:a 16k

The transients in st44 make the encoder use eight short windows; -aac_pns and
-aac_is make it use noise substitution and intensity stereo; M/S, TNS and pulses
appear as the encoder finds them useful (aac_fixture_test.go logs the counts).

The fuzz seeds in ../fuzz/FuzzAAC* are frames and headers cut from these files,
and a few AudioSpecificConfig byte strings.

ref/ holds what ffmpeg 9.0.2 (Homebrew, arm64, Apple clang 21) decodes them to with
its C code paths, as float32 little-endian, interleaved (the oracle of TestAACOracle):

  ffmpeg -cpuflags 0 -i st44.aac -f f32le ref/st44.f32           (likewise st44-tools,
  mono22, mono8)
  ffmpeg -cpuflags 0 -i surround51.aac -frames:a 12 -f f32le ref/surround51.f32
